NEW_SECTION
    #cacheTable td:nth-child(2){color:var(--amber); white-space:nowrap}
    #cacheTable td:nth-child(3){color:var(--muted)}

    /* scroll state table: same look as the cache table, value column in amber */
    #scrollTable{width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-family:var(--mono); font-size:.8rem}
    #scrollTable th{text-align:left; color:var(--dim); font-weight:500; font-size:.7rem; letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase; padding:0 8px 8px 0}
    #scrollTable td{border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding:8px 8px 8px 0; vertical-align:top; overflow-wrap:anywhere}
    #scrollTable td:first-child{color:var(--fg); white-space:nowrap}
    @media (max-width:720px){ #scrollTable td:first-child{white-space:normal} }
    #scrollTable td:nth-child(2){color:var(--amber); white-space:nowrap}
    #scrollTable td:nth-child(3){color:var(--muted)}
    /* a restore that landed is good news: green, not the red of the cache table's drop flash */
    #scrollTable tr.flash td{animation:restored 1.2s ease-out}
    @keyframes restored{from{background:rgba(80,220,140,.18)} to{background:transparent}}
    #cacheTable tr.flash td{animation:flash .9s ease-out}
    @keyframes flash{from{background:rgba(255,107,127,.18)} to{background:transparent}}

REASON
Styles for the scroll state table, matching the cache table; the reading column stays on one line at desktop width (wraps on phones), and a restore flashes green rather than the red used for a cache drop.

